# Files to exclude from convention-sync (one glob per line)
# Patterns match against relative paths like: commands/foo.sh, rules/bar.mdc

# WIP commands
commands/hudl.md
commands/github-pr-hudl.sh

# --- Maestro flows -----------------------------------------------------------
# The build-and-test harness ships ONE canonical, reusable flow a fresh machine
# needs — capture-buy-quote.sh defaults to skills/build-and-test/maestro/
# buy-quote-input.yaml — so buy-quote*.yaml MUST keep syncing.
#
# Task/feature-specific flows an agent authors mid-run (e.g. the Maya swap-*
# flows) are GUI dev artifacts, NOT agent conventions. Keep them LOCALLY for
# reuse, but never push them to the agent repo. Until the orchestration
# "where do per-task yamls live" strategy is finalized, list those task-flow
# families here so the leak can't recur.
skills/build-and-test/maestro/swap-*.yaml

# Third-party skills need no entry here: skills/ is authored-only (the sync
# excludes and REPORTS anything the repo does not carry and whose SKILL.md
# claims no author the repo distributes). Listing one here only hides it from
# that report. Use this file for paths that ARE the operator's but should stay
# local, and for a secret-scan false positive.

# Sync announcement mechanic: machine-local by decision, not distributed. These
# resolve which session wrote each file the sync carries, and compose the
# #edge-dev-agents commit announcement. Both are this box's habit rather than
# part of the setup a second Mac reproduces, and the announcement has no reason
# to announce changes to its own announcer.
skills/convention-sync/scripts/sync-*.sh
